Comparison-only fault overlay; frozen snapshot is the baseline, never edited.

Adopts the four-control base without changing its existing runtime hooks.
Differences from production: reset is RKVENC2-only (production's is generic MPP);
hang precedes IOMMU when both are armed; IOMMU uses fixed 0xfffff000, the real
registered domain/device and the real handler (not physical fault IRQ delivery).
Production mpp_rkvenc2.c actually passes NULL as domain; we deliberately do not.
Delay is after DONE-list detachment with the transferred job reference, outside
the session mutex, rather than before production's pending-list removal.
PID identity is task_pid_nr(current), equal to production current->pid, not TGID.

Added checks precede attachment/IRQ/clock/session-state publication and retain
the existing identity-unlock and PM-put error paths. Session injection belongs
only to validated initial RKVENC INIT_CLIENT_TYPE, never open(). No new locks,
session fields, activation references or register leases are introduced.
Superseded base lines: Kconfig's four-control help only; headers are additive.
README supersessions and fixture proof limits are recorded in fault-injection/README.md.
